1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,717
YAMU!

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,440
You're on the move!

4
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:07,920
I've activated the
autopilot, so let's do this.

5
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:12,960
Oh, I love this part of the job.

6
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,080
Woo-hoo!

7
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:23,320
Last one there's got to polish me boots.

8
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,560
Give it a wrap, Balan.

9
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:43,565
Seeing these carvings confirms
what I suspected all along, Yuki.

10
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:47,500
You share a common bond with
a 5,000-year-old pharaoh.

11
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,437
Do you know what this means?

12
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:52,337
Yeah, that my life's more
confusing than most kids.

13
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:55,037
Perhaps I can shed more
light on the subject.

14
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:58,377
I've spent the latter part of my
career studying dual monsters.

15
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,660
It started as more than a game.

16
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:06,140
Egyptian sorcerers discovered a way to seal
real monsters away within stone tablets.

17
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:11,011
They would periodically release these
monsters to display their great power.

18
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:13,480
As more monsters were collected,

19
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,000
the sorcerers' powers grew stronger,

20
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,837
until eventually this
shadow magic spun out of

21
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:21,980
control and threatened to
destroy all life on Earth.

22
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:26,497
But one man was able to face this
madness and turn the darkness to light.

23
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:30,300
The great pharaoh whose power
you carry around your neck.

24
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:33,837
How does that explain
what's happening now?

25
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,617
Did these ancient monsters
come back or something?

26
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:41,040
I'm afraid so, but there's another
piece to this story you need to know.

27
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,674
Ever hear of the lost city of Atlantis?

28
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,400
I read a great book about it once. What?

29
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,700
You nerd.

30
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:52,677
In my latest expedition, I may
have discovered that very city.

31
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,880
An underwater world that existed
long before ancient Egypt.

32
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:01,320
But what really puzzled me were
the carvings I saw on the walls.

33
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,260
Take a look.

34
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:05,840
No way!

35
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,100
Duel monsters!

36
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,410
Precisely.

37
00:03:09,493 --> 00:03:12,977
So these monsters didn't originate
5,000 years ago in Egypt.

38
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:16,257
They lived over 10,000 years ago in what I

39
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:19,000
believe to be the
legendary city of Atlantis.

40
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,577
Atlantis was real?

41
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,800
Do you know what this means?

42
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:25,900
Your discovery could
completely rewrite history.

43
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,694
There's still quite a bit I don't know.

44
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,260
Look at this.

45
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,365
Looks like the monsters
are attacking the city.

46
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:37,977
If you look at the picture more closely,

47
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:41,797
you'll notice that only some of the
monsters are destroying the city.

48
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,920
Hey, you're right. So,

49
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,025
if only some of these
monsters seem to be evil,

50
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,217
does that mean that the
other monsters are good?

51
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,400
I haven't collected enough
evidence to confirm that,

52
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:58,060
but I believe there's a parallel world of
monsters that exists alongside our world.

53
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:02,617
And throughout history, certain humans
have been able to release these monsters.

54
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,641
Some of them have helped mankind.

55
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,000
Others have tried to destroy it.

56
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,520
Give me a break, you nutty professor!

57
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:11,890
No!

58
00:04:11,973 --> 00:04:13,680
The pain! Good!

59
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,217
Because that's my grandfather
you're talking about!

60
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,640
You got that, punk?

61
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,580
Anyone who messes with him messes with me.

62
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,840
So keep your comments to yourself.

63
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,660
Won't happen again.

64
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,010
Don't worry.

65
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:27,827
I'm no stranger to ridicule.

66
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:30,760
Besides, it is a bit of
a far-fetched theory.

67
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:31,900
But it's true.

68
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,980
I believe you, Professor.

69
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,390
Figures.

70
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,941
After all the weird stuff we've
been through, I'd believe anything.

71
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:45,077
Like the time I fought
Maric in that Shadow game.

72
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:48,100
All those monster attacks
felt pretty real to me.

73
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,477
And did you forget the times that both Mai

74
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:53,157
and Bakura got blasted
into the Shadow Realm?

75
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:57,257
Let's face it, there's plenty of stuff
out there that can't be explained.

76
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,077
Like how there's a pharaoh
living in my puzzle.

77
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:00,990
Actually,

78
00:05:01,073 --> 00:05:03,577
our hypothesis suggests that
the supernatural phenomena

79
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:06,895
you experience may actually
find its roots in Atlantis.

80
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:11,717
Whoa, those are some pretty big words,
especially coming from such a little kid.

81
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,960
A kid?

82
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,417
I'm a college student,
thank you very much.

83
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,600
College student?

84
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,060
My granddaughter is quite gifted.

85
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:23,640
Oh, Grandpa, I'm just your
average child genius. Genius.

86
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,377
Cannon.

87
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:29,197
Very impressive, but
can't you spell obnoxious?

88
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,360
I heard that!

89
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:34,020
Now, Rebecca, is that the
behavior of a college student?

90
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,000
Sorry, Gramps, go on.

91
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:39,597
Now, the point that I'm
trying to make here is this.

92
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:44,100
When Egyptian sorcerers conjured
these monsters 5,000 years ago,

93
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:47,555
the pharaoh was there to save
mankind from destruction.

94
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:51,420
Now it seems that pharaoh's
been reborn in you,

95
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,620
which could mean mankind
needs his help again.

96
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:58,897
Yeah, but I wouldn't even know
where to begin, Professor.

97
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:03,392
I mean, do we try and get all these
monsters to go back to their own world?

98
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:09,232
Or should we focus on finding out what
that weird motorcycle gang is up to?

99
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:13,445
Unfortunately, this is where my
knowledge of the situation ends.

100
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:15,440
Wait a sec.

101
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:17,120
I may have a clue.

102
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:20,180
Ever see anything like this before?

103
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,440
That's awesome.

104
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,665
What have you got there, Yugi?

105
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,130
Not sure.

106
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:29,518
The guys we dueled against
last night left it behind.

107
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,860
Hmm, incredible.

108
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:35,851
This stone is remarkably similar to
something I discovered on my expedition.

109
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,884
Would you mind if I held
on to this stone, Yugi?

110
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,786
No, of course not, Professor.

111
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:50,037
I'd like to take it back to my lab.

112
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:54,002
I have a feeling it may hold the
answers to many of our questions.

113
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,840
You kids, be careful.

114
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:02,259
I'm going to take Arthur
and Rebecca to the airport.

115
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:04,660
Goodbye, cutie.

116
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:08,430
Ta-ta!

117
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,540
Good riddance.

118
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,337
Just when I thought things
were getting back to normal,

119
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,538
they went and got ten times weirder.

120
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:21,802
Yes, and this time the situation
seems more treacherous than ever.

121
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:24,000
Please, help me.

122
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,300
Hey, you all right there, Yook? Weird.

123
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,619
Did you hear someone call for help?

124
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:34,360
Nah, this place is a ghost town.

125
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:35,441
Don't say ghost.

126
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,317
Come on, it's been an
exhausting day, guys.

127
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,200
Let's go catch some zees.

128
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,720
Easy for you to say.

129
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,649
After that story, it's going
to be nightmare central for me.

130
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:57,220
There's a world of monsters
that exists alongside our world.

131
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,440
Can't sleep, can you?

132
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,230
Nope.

133
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:06,657
Right now, all I can think about
is what Professor Hawkins said.

134
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:08,540
I feel the same way, Yugi.

135
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:12,260
If his theory about these
duel monsters is true,

136
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,860
this could be our toughest fight yet.

137
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,760
We located the Pharaoh Master.

138
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,397
Unfortunately, we weren't
able to capture his soul.

139
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:35,760
I didn't expect you to
defeat him this soon.

140
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,980
We've just begun.

141
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:38,792
But you know me, Master.

142
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,200
I never come back empty-handed.

143
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:46,710
Excellent.

144
00:08:46,793 --> 00:08:48,480
The Egyptian gods.

145
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:54,440
At long last, I've waited an eternity
to hold their power in my hands.

146
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:03,780
I finally possess the supreme force
necessary to awaken the great beast.

147
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:12,040
Soon we shall rid the earth of mankind
and rebuild civilization as it once was.

148
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:19,520
Serpents of the Orachalcos,
please hear my call.

149
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,240
I offer thee the gods of Egypt.

150
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:28,040
Use their divine might to unlock the
sacred chamber of the great beast.

151
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:32,440
Awaken him from his ancient
slumber by accepting my offering.

152
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:46,117
The time has arrived, my friends.

153
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:52,080
Finally, after 10,000 years, the
great leviathan shall rise again.

154
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:59,760
Pharaoh, we need you.

155
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,480
Help us.

156
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,900
Someone needs us.

157
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:11,240
Yeah, but where are they?

158
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,960
Please, where are you?

159
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,390
There it is again.

160
00:10:16,473 --> 00:10:17,500
Pharaoh! This way.

161
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,390
Help!

162
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:23,525
Whoever that is, they
could be almost anywhere.

163
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,300
Can you hear me?

164
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:27,360
Any ideas?

165
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:30,080
Let's split up and search. Got it.

166
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:34,450
Hello?

167
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,480
Anyone here?

168
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:44,761
How are we supposed to
find someone in this place?

169
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,920
There's way too many doorways.

170
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,260
It's Karibu!

171
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,840
What's he doing here?

172
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:57,157
Maybe he's trying to lead us
to whoever needs our help.

173
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,070
Let's go.

174
00:10:58,620 --> 00:10:59,450
Right.

175
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:10,380
This must be it.

176
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:15,790
Be careful.

177
00:11:15,873 --> 00:11:17,859
Who knows what's on the other side?

178
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,790
Wow.

179
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:29,240
I've never seen this one before.

180
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:30,620
Nor have I.

181
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,400
So stay close by.

182
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,640
Pharaoh, are you in here?

183
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,220
Follow the sound of my voice.

184
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:40,860
This way!

185
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,620
What's happening?

186
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,080
This is weird.

187
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,200
Where are we?

188
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:04,380
Hmm, it appears to be
some kind of kingdom.

189
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:09,840
Yugi, we're not alone.

190
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:14,260
Whatever it is, it
doesn't look too friendly.

191
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,600
Told you!

192
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:33,300
Do you see what I see? Yes.

193
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,500
Some sort of statues made of crystal.

194
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:40,140
They appear to be dragons.

195
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,180
They're huge!

196
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,465
I'm glad they're only statues.

197
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,220
You're here!

198
00:12:58,100 --> 00:12:59,760
I knew you'd find me!

199
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,120
You're a dark magician, girl!

200
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,017
Tell us, why were you
calling out for help?

201
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,880
Pharaoh, both of our worlds are in danger.

202
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:11,180
And without your help, we
will all cease to exist.

203
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:12,390
But how?

204
00:13:12,473 --> 00:13:13,380
Wait!

205
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,680
So Professor Hawkins was right!

206
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,520
As long as mankind has walked the earth,

207
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:23,057
the dominion of the beasts has existed
side by side with the human world.

208
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:25,846
We have lived this way
for thousands of years.

209
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:30,687
Although our worlds are separate, we
depend on one another in order to survive.

210
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:35,117
But now something is threatening
that survival and it must be stopped.

211
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:40,260
A gateway between us has opened and now
the great beast will swallow us all.

212
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,740
It lives above the sky,

213
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:48,320
feasting on the life force of monsters
and humans, as it did in the past.

214
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:52,937
We need you.

215
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,700
All of us need you.

216
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:02,080
If this continues, we'll be gone forever.

217
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:05,760
You too are our only hope. We'll help.

218
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,217
Yeah, but how?

219
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:10,620
What are we supposed to do
to stop this giant monster?

220
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:19,680
These three dragons once served
as the protectors of my world.

221
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:24,060
They defeated the great beast 10,000
years ago when it first appeared.

222
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,182
But for this, they paid a price.

223
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:31,860
Now they're frozen in time, unable to
defend my dominion as they did so long ago.

224
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,100
But how can we help?

225
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:40,077
the legend states that
three brave warriors will

226
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,925
awaken these dragons when
they are needed again

227
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:47,957
pharaoh i believe that one of these
warriors is you and if i'm correct

228
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:54,257
you will be able to remove that sword
from the ice and what will happen

229
00:14:54,340 --> 00:14:59,357
if you're wrong i'm not wrong i know
that you once saved egypt from the

230
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:05,620
shadow games and i believe you can
do the same for us ready yugi yeah

231
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,880
Okay, did it work or not?

232
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,200
I guess so.

233
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:42,700
You've released Timaeus.

234
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:45,120
Now, according to the prophecy,

235
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:49,117
you and Timaeus will become linked
together as soon as you call his name.

236
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,480
Well, here goes.

237
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:52,170
Timaeus!

238
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:57,160
It's worked.

239
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,620
Now join forces.

240
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:06,800
I can feel its power surging through me.

241
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:12,780
I can't take much more!

242
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,640
Is it morning already?

243
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,300
Wait a sec.

244
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,678
That's not the sun!

245
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:32,050
Grandpa!

246
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:33,121
What's going on?

247
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:36,006
The monsters seem to be
trapped in that light.

248
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,613
Oh, no, it's happening.

249
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,100
Yuki, what's happening?

250
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,280
What is that thing?

251
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,230
Yuki!

252
00:16:50,313 --> 00:16:51,691
Things are getting worse.

253
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:54,098
Or at least they're getting weirder.

254
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:56,437
Yeah, any idea what that is up there?

255
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,780
I think I do, and it's not good.

256
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:12,740
What's that?

257
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,371
I don't want to find out.

258
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:22,920
Now, great Leviathan, time to show the
Pharaoh what true power is all about.

259
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,900
Oh, guys, run!

260
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,350
Yogi!

261
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:34,420
Come on!

262
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,560
Yu-Gi, no!

263
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,420
It's that dragon we released!

264
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:53,740
Now I summon Timaeus!

265
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,100
Look at the size of that thing!

266
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:08,920
Tamaeus, protect us from that monster!

267
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:44,800
No, this is impossible.

268
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:02,480
We did it.

269
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,000
We've only just begun.

270
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:12,740
The Great Beast is still weak,
so he retreated for the moment.

271
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:17,000
And for that, my companions and
I are truly grateful, my Pharaoh.

272
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:20,580
But many of us remain
prisoners on the other side.

273
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:22,520
What's next?

274
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:27,160
The Great Beast will return
again, and his power will grow.

275
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,305
He must be stopped before
he is fully restored.

276
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:32,180
Time is running out!

277
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:45,455
It seems like Timaeus is
strong, but not strong enough.

278
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,940
We must release the other two dragons.
